<title>USA: AGA says U.S. weekly natgas stocks fell 161 bcf.</title>
<headline>AGA says U.S. weekly natgas stocks fell 161 bcf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Gas Association</p>
<p>estimates of U.S. working gas in storage in billion cubic feet</p>
<p>(bcf):		    01/31/97  01/24/97  Net Chg  Pct Full(6)</p>
<p> Producing Reg. (1)	  298     334	-36     33</p>
<p> Consuming Reg. East (2)   838     954     -116     47</p>
<p> Consuming Reg. West (3)   213     222	 -9     44</p>
<p> Total U.S.		   1349    1510     -161     42</p>
<p>Notes: (1) Incl Texas, Okla., Kansas, N.Mexico, Arkansas, Louisiana, and Miss. (2) Incl states east of Miss. River less Miss., plus Iowa, Neb and Missouri (3) Incl states west of the Miss. River less producing region and Iowa, Neb and Missouri.</p>
<p>Survey sample and full working gas estimates</p>
<p> -			 Survey Sample   Est. Full Work-    Yr-Ago</p>
<p> -			 Size--Pct (4)   ing Gas--BCF (5)   Week</p>
<p> Producing Region	    71		    908	   353</p>
<p> Consuming Region East     95		   1790	   680</p>
<p> Consuming Region West     96		    482	   271</p>
<p> Total U.S.		    88		   3180	  1304</p>
<p>Notes: (4) Ratio of max WG vol. to est. of highest WG in storage in past 2 yrs (EIA).(5) Highest WG level by state added to give regional and national levels (EIA).(6) Regional and total vols divided by est.full regional and total vols.</p>
</text>
